  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Heads up – watch the coach's signs",
  "description": "Spread cones over an area of about 20 × 20 metres. Everyone has a ball and dribbles freely between and around the cones in different ways: inside, outside, sole and both feet. The coach stands at the side and says nothing – instead they give signals with their arms.\n\nArm straight up: stop and put your foot on the ball. Arm circling: turn 180 degrees and dribble back at full speed for a few metres. Arm pointing one way: dribble that way. Both arms crossed: do a feint at the nearest cone. Anyone who misses a signal has not looked up – that is the whole point of the game.\n\nVariants: decide which foot or which touches to use, or add more signals, such as a change of pace or a particular feint. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up between touches – feel the ball, don't watch it all the time."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Small touches in tight spaces, longer ones when there is room."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Sole on the ball as soon as the arm goes up – stand still and in control."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Turn with the ball close to your foot and speed up after the turn."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
